course: dictionary
lesson: 13716
title: Instinctive: done without thinking
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Something instinctive is done naturally, without learning it or stopping to think first. The word comes from instinct, the feeling inside you that tells you what to do. «Mia pulled her hand away from the hot pan before she even thought about it.» That was an instinctive reaction.
explain: Animals have many instincts that they are born with. «A young spider spins a web the first time it tries, with no one to show it how.» Spinning a web is instinctive behaviour. A dog learning to sit is different: that is learned behaviour, because someone has to teach it.
explain: A quick test: did someone have to teach you how to do it? If not, it may be instinctive. «Baby turtles crawl straight towards the sea.» Nobody taught them, so that is instinctive behaviour too.
explain: The adverb is instinctively, which means in an instinctive way. «Tom ducked instinctively when the ball flew at his head.» He did not plan it or think it through; his body simply reacted.
fact: Instinctive means done naturally, without learning or thinking about it.
fact: In science, instinctive behaviour is something an animal is born knowing how to do.
fact: Birds migrating, babies sucking and turtles heading for the sea are all examples of instinctive behaviour.
fact: Learned behaviour, like a dog learning tricks, has to be taught or practised.
fact: Useful phrases: instinctive reaction, instinctive behaviour, an instinctive feeling.
exercise: «Sam ducked the moment the ball flew at him.» What kind of reaction was this? | *An instinctive reaction | A learned trick | A slow, careful plan | A reaction he had practised for weeks
exercise: A spider spins its web the first time it tries, with no one to show it how. Is this instinctive behaviour or learned behaviour? | Copied from its mum | Learned at school | *Instinctive behaviour | Learned behaviour
exercise: Which word means done naturally, without learning it or thinking about it? | Planned | Practised | *Instinctive | Taught
test: «Baby turtles crawl straight to the sea.» Why is this instinctive? | *They are born knowing how to do it | They saw it on television | They were taught by their parents | They learned it at school
test: «Lily instinctively covered her ears when the fire alarm rang.» What does instinctively mean? | In a way she had been taught in class | In a loud way | *In a natural way, without thinking | In a slow, careful way
exam: Which sentence shows learned behaviour rather than instinctive behaviour? | A baby sucks milk straight away | *A dog learns to sit when its owner shows it how | Birds migrate south every autumn | Turtles head for the sea after hatching
